	title = {Systematics and distribution patterns of the {Balkan} species of {Eryngium} ( {Apiaceae} , {Saniculoideae} )},
	volume = {12},
	abstract = {The Balkan species of genus Eryngium (Apiaceae, Saniculoideae) are 11 in number distributed over six sections. Sectional classification of the genus in the Balkans is presented here. Although most of these sections are common to adjacent Anatolia (except for the endemic E. sect. Astrantiifolia), only three widespread species actually grow in both regions. Distribution maps of each Balkan species are supplied. Ecological aspects proved useful for their understanding. Most Balkan species of Eryngium are fairly old (except for the widespread ones) and obviously result from early immigration and evolution in the region},
