	title = {How to peer review a manuscript},
	abstract = {Peer review is an activity central to increasing the quality of communication in the health sciences, but almost no formal or standardised training for peer reviewers exists. In this chapter we provide a series of practical tips on how to peer review a manuscript and write the report based on the evidence from evidence-based peer r published research that is summarised elsewhere in this book, and on our combined experience of reviewing for approximately 30 journals. Overall, we believe that the best way to increase the quality of peer reviewing would be to conduct such reviews based on up to date evidence – an approach we call peer review.},
