	abstract = {The structure and canopy composition of successional scrub dominated by broom Cytisus scoparius, elder Sambucus nigra, gorse Ulex europaeus and mahoe Melicytus ramiflorus was measured. Eight stands in Hoon Hay valley were arranged in order of increasing age which corresponded to a toposequence from dry sites on upper north facing slopes to moist sites on lower south facing slopes. The latest expansion of elder began c.12 yr ago when it colonised young broom stands. Broom dies by c.15 yr leaving elder, which in turn is invaded by mahoe. Broom and elder are desirable species where the aim of vegetation management is to re-establish native forest in this region.-from Author},
